mb-creg-belief-scoring
----------------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code, data or
weights.

Paper (method idea credited)
----------------------------
Ranulfo Bezerra and Kimitoshi Yamazaki.
"A Benchmark and Layered Evaluation Protocol for Evidence-Grounded Shared
Belief Updating in Connected Robotics". arXiv:2611.11842, v1, submitted
9 Nov 2026. Primary category cs.RO, cross-listed cs.AI, cs.CL and cs.MA.
CREG (Connected Robotics Evidence Graph) Benchmark is the benchmark's name
in the abstract, not the title.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.11842 (project page https://creg-bench.github.io/)
Licence: arXiv non-exclusive distribution licence,
http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/ (a paper licence, not a
software grant).

Code: the project page links the GitHub repository
RanulfoBezerra/Evidence-Graph-Toolkit and names an MIT License in its
footer. That repository returned GitHub 404 when fetched on 2026-11-13, so
its licence file, HEAD SHA and contents are UNVERIFIED. No upstream code,
scenario, reference, prompt or data was used.

Method only: the idea of scoring an evidence-to-belief trajectory at every
evidence prefix (posterior, support and contradict sets, contradiction
flag, admissible next action) against an independently computed normative
reference, and of a relation-content ablation. The update, staleness,
supersession, contradiction, action and expiry rules, the oracle, the
fixtures and the baselines are this sketch's own. No text, figures, tables
or data from the paper are copied into the code; the PDF was not read; no
model or benchmark run was re-run. The paper's claims appear only in
paper_evidence.json, quoted and marked UNVERIFIED.
